Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------

liblinear-rs is a Rust port and reimplementation of LIBLINEAR, a library
for large linear classification and regression, originally created and
maintained by the LIBLINEAR Project:

    R.-E. Fan, K.-W. Chang, C.-J. Hsieh, X.-R. Wang and C.-J. Lin
    Department of Computer Science, National Taiwan University
    https://www.csie.ntu.edu.tw/~cjlin/liblinear

    LIBLINEAR: A Library for Large Linear Classification.
    Journal of Machine Learning Research 9 (2008), 1871-1874.

The Rust implementation targets numerical equivalence with upstream
LIBLINEAR, shown by the parity checks in this repository; it is not a
bitwise-identical copy.

The solvers, input shapes and reference behavior derive from LIBLINEAR,
which is distributed under the BSD 3-Clause License. The original
copyright of The LIBLINEAR Project is retained and is not superseded by
the Rust port's copyright.

